onical-instruction-vector`**: in this step replace that call site's function with a 3-line private copy? No — rule: `semantic.cljc` is deleted in 8f-3, so step 4 would break it. Therefore step 4 is split: **4a** (R5 `:push` edits and the `rule_r_test` deftest removal) lands in 8f-1; **4b** (shrinking `ucf.cljc`, deleting `ucf_test.cljc`) moves to 8f-3 and is the first `git rm`/edit of that slice, in the same commit as `semantic.cljc`'s deletion. Lane for 4a: `yin.vm.rule-r-test`, `yin.vm.semantic-register.scan-test`, `dao.space.query-test`.\n\n**Step 5 — gate for 8f-1.** `clj -M:kondo` (no new warnings; the deleted files' warnings vanish), `bb test:clj` quick tier, then Node and Dart lanes per `build-n-test.md` (clean `lib/cljd-out` first). Report with: the deleted-test ledger (handoff/checkpoint: 0 deftests, already gone in 8d; `completion_test` 19 deleted, table in R3 as the replacement column; `rule_r_test` 1 deleted; `scan_test` 1 deleted; `cell_test` 1 deleted; `query_test` 1 deleted; `publish_test` 0 deleted, 1 narrowed), the pinned literals before/after, deftest count before/after.\n\nCommit shape for 8f-1: one commit, `refactor(yin.vm): the stack grammar is debruijn-code's own data; old transport sources, dependency completion and the v3 footprint residue are out (8f-1)`. Architect sign-off before commit, as standing.\n\n## 3. What must wait\n\n- **8f-2** (plan Q3 commit 1): `git mv` `semantic_register*` → `semantic*`, tests likewise. Unchanged by this ruling.\n- **8f-3** (plan Q3 commit 2 plus the deletions): `git rm semantic.cljc linearize.cljc code.cljc`, `semantic_test` (25) `linearize_test` (23) `code_test` (13), **plus step 4b** (`ucf.cljc` shrink, `ucf_test` 24), the three demos, `test_utils.cljc` (`create-vm` is already the walker; `run-encoder-session:167` and the `linearize`/`semantic` requires go), the ~38 test requirers incl. the 9 C4 files, `ucf/remote_test`, the ports of `semantic_engine_test`/`semantic_ffi_test`/`semantic_stream_observer_test`