tic.cljc` is retained. They die in 8f-3 in the same commit as `semantic.cljc`, `semantic_test` and `linearize.cljc`. The 8f-3 ledger gains: `vm.cljc:612-680` (`opcode-table` :619, `opcase` :647). The optimisation note `yin/vm/docs/bytecode-vm-optimization.md:336` that mentions `vm/opcase` is 8g's.\n\n**D2 — `query_test/segment-db` kept for `code-joins-store-put-key-to-ast-by-value`: CONFIRMED, with the disposition for 8f-3 fixed now.** My ruling enumerated two callers; the third is real (`query_test:1855-1866`). The old-code dependency in that test is exactly two things: `code/project-segment-qualified` (the v3 positional segment projection) and `linearize/lower-rows` (the v3 lowerer), both in `segment-db` (`query_test:1813-1818`). The test itself asserts a dao.space fact (U6: a `$ast`/`$code` join by value across relations that share no ids), not an old-kernel fact, so it must be PORTED in 8f-3, not dropped. The port is mechanical: `segment-db` becomes `(rel (scan/segment-rows (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast))))` (`scan/segment-rows` is the v4 twin, ruling fact 6), and because the register `:store-put` row carries `rd` before `key` (`semantic_register/code.cljc:45`, row shape `[a pc :store-put rd key value]`) the pattern changes from `[$code _ _ :store-put ?key _]` to `[$code _ _ :store-put _ ?key & _]`. With that, the `yin.vm.code` and `yin.vm.linearize` requires of `query_test` go in 8f-3. Retaining instead of porting in 8f-1 is the right call under minimal diff: 8f-3 already edits `query_test` for the same two requires, and a new v4 join assertion belongs in the slice whose three-host lane validates the register path.\n\n**D3 — completion_test had 18 deftests, not 19: CONFIRMED; nothing else vanished.** `git show HEAD:test/yin/vm/completion_test.cljc` contains 18 `(deftest` forms; my 19 was a miscount. Name-set diff over `test/**/*.{clj,cljc,cljs,cljd}` (HEAD vs working tree, same extraction both sides, 4396 → 4374 by my regex; the engineer's regex gave 4440 → 4418; both deltas −22):\n\n- removed, 24 names: the 18 completion_test names (`blocked-reader-wait-entry-is-a-root`, `caller-fetch-answers-what-the-vm-does-not-hold`, `code-facts-from-tree-and-segment-are-equal`, `code-side-missing-pid-is-incomplete`, `def-recursion-terminates`, `early-refusals`, `env-binding-does-not-discharge-a-free-name`, `ffi-pair-key-operand-is-refused`, `host-functions-in-values`, `loaded-images-answer-fetch`, `module-names`, `present-parked-record-is-pulled`, `primitive-without-a-profile-is-incomplete`, `segment-free-names-cases`, `stored-closure-is-a-work-item-and-its-names-are-discharged`, `two-closures-one-segment-two-envs`, `unfetchable-segment-blocks-and-the-rest-is-walked`, `value-side-missing-pid-is-refused`); the four single deletions `canonicalize-verifies-the-batch-stamp` (rule_r), `completion-address-reuse-preserves-answers` (scan), `completion-over-a-cell-is-not-complete-test` (cell), `requirement-sets-from-tree-and-segment-are-equal` (query); and the two renamed names `footprint-mnemonics-is-the-v3-table-minus-push`, `opcode-table-derives-from-the-named-table`.\n- added, 2 names: `footprint-mnemonics-is-the-v4-table`, `opcode-table-is-this-dimensions-own-data`.\n\n24 − 2 = 22. Every removed name is accounted for by the ruling's ledger; no deftest outside it disappeared.\n\n## 3. Findings\n\n**P1 (blocking):** none.\n\n**P2 (should fix before commit):** none.\n\n**P3 (nits; fix in 8f-1 if the orchestrator wants a clean slice, otherwise ledgered):**\n\n1. `test/yin/vm/linker/publish_test.cljc:173` — the deftest is still named `published-footprint-completes-module-discovery` but now asserts only that the published manifest carries `[:yin.module/footprint :effects]` = `#{}`. The name describes the dropped `completion/complete` fact. Suggested name: `published-manifest-carries-the-footprint-effects`.\n2. `test/yin/vm/debruijn_code_test.cljc:338,345` — `(is (not (contains? dc/opcode-table :var)))` appears twice (my ruling prescribed it in the new first block while the kept second block already had it). Harmless duplication; drop the first.\n3. `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf.cljc:326` — the `parking-kinds` docstring names `yin.vm.ucf.handoff`, deleted in this slice. R6 says a docstring naming a deleted var is fixed in the deleting step; `parking-kinds` itself dies in 8f-3 step 4b, so deletion there is an acceptable fix. Ledger it for 8f-3 (and 8g's grep gate) if not touched now.\n4. `test/yin/vm/linker_test.cljc:263,315` — prose says `yin.vm.code/materialize-vector!` / `yin.vm.code`; the file's `code` alias is already `yin.vm.semantic-register.code` (:22). My R4 missed these two prose sites. Fix with 8f-3's `yin.vm.code` deletion (or in the 8f-2 rename, where the alias target moves anyway).\n5. `src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows/checkpoint.cljc:4` says it \"replaces `yin.vm.ucf.checkpoint`\", now historical prose. 8g.\n\nVerification status as reported by the engineer and not re-run here: JVM quick tier 4068 tests / 251041 assertions / 0 failures with `-e :slow`, kondo diagnostics unchanged against a frozen baseline. Node and Dart lanes are unrun; the three-host lane (`pinned-identities-are-host-independent`, `register-determinism`) is the ruling's landing gate and the standing commit rule (sign-off + green lanes), so the orchestrator runs them before committing. Nothing in this diff is host-specific beyond what those lanes already cover.\n\n## 4. Ledger additions for 8f-3 (from this review)\n\n- Delete `vm.cljc` `opcode-table` (:619) and `opcase` (:647) with `semantic.cljc` (D1).\n- Port `query_test/segment-db` to `scan/segment-rows` over `sr-linearize/project` and change the join pattern to `[$code _ _ :store-put _ ?key & _]`; then drop `yin.vm.code` and `yin.vm.linearize` from `query_test` (D2).\n- Fix or delete the stale prose at `ucf.cljc:326`, `linker_test.cljc:263,315`.\n\n## 5. Invariants\n\nA is the only code identity: unchanged, H stays a derived checksum. Tree always available: completion's tree-less segment scoping is what died; the scanner's agreement tests still compare against the tree. Derive, don't persist: the one new literal replaces a derivation whose source dies; no new table beyond the private `terminators` set. Minimal diff: 73 insertions against 5794 deletions, zero new namespaces. No backend widening: 23 mnemonics in, 23 out, `lowering-contract-version` stays 2.\n\nSIGN-OFF\nCreated-GMT: 2026-10-15 09:50:28 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-15 16:50:28 +07\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-10-15 09:55:00 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-15 16:55:00 +07\nCoding-Agent: claude (claude-fable-5-1)\nSession-ID: pending\nBrief: ./collab/1793100000000-architect-8f3-nan-ruling.prompt.md\nBranch: srvm-phase8f3 @ 7b8d2a93 (no source edits; probe test ns created and deleted; tree clean apart from collab/)\n\n# Architect ruling: 8f-3 Node+Dart `noncanonical-registers` on NaN programs\n\n## 1. Verdict\n\nRoot cause confirmed by reading the code and by a JVM probe. It is the\nhypothesised bug class: §3.4 item 13 (`canonical-projection` in\n`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/code.cljc`, lines 815 and 820) compares a\nre-projected tuple against the loaded tuple with host `=`, whole tuple,\nliteral operands included. The re-projection copies every literal operand by\nreference (`with-registers`, line 703, `:else (nth t (inc i))`), so the two\ntuples hold the *same* NaN. The JVM's `=` short-circuits on reference identity\n(`Util.equiv`: `k1 == k2`) and passes. On JS a NaN is a primitive: `identical?`\nis `===`, false for NaN, and the number `-equiv` is also false. On Dart `=` on\ndoubles is IEEE `==`, false for NaN. So the check reports the first tuple that\ncarries a NaN literal as `:noncanonical-registers` at its pc. The two failing\ntests put `##NaN` straight into the test form (`(py/float (data/float-value\n##NaN))`, int_ops_test.cljc 402-412 and 533-536), which lowers to a\n`[:const rd ##NaN]` tuple; pc 1600/1601 is the first such tuple after the\nprelude. ±inf, -0.0 and large floats are NOT part of this defect: they are\nreflexive under `=` on all three hosts.\n\nThis passed in 8e only because the `:semantic` runner then ran the old kernel,\nwhose loader had no item 13. Nothing about the Python prelude changed.\n\n## 2. Evidence (JVM probe, throwaway ns `yin.vm.nan-probe-test`, deleted)\n\n```\nA  well-formed? [[:const 0 ##NaN] [:halt 0]]                 -> nil   (shared box; JVM identity)\nA2 well-formed? NaN in a body and inside a data literal      -> nil   (same reason)\nB  (= [:const 0 nanA] [:const 0 nanB]), distinct boxes        -> false (JVM = is not NaN-reflexive either; only identity saves it)\nC  (cbor/content= [:const 0 nanA] [:const 0 nanB])            -> true\nD  (cbor/content= t (copy t)) for every mnemonic in §2.3,\n   incl. symbols, keyword ops, [regs], bool, nil buffer, str,\n   bigint literal                                             -> true for all 22 shapes (no refusal, no throw)\nE  nested distinct NaNs in {:k} and [...] with ±inf, -0.0,\n   #{} , \"s\", 1/2, 1.5M: content= true, host = false\nF  content= keeps -0.0 apart from 0.0 (host = merges them);  int vs float stays apart\nG  semantic/load-vector + vm/run of [[:const 0 ##NaN] [:halt 0]] -> value ##NaN   (kernel executes NaN fine)\nH  reload of the identical vector into the same machine      -> :ok\nI  reload of a content-equal vector with a FRESH NaN box      -> throws \"Cannot load segment: the id already holds different code\"\n```\n\nProbe I exposes a second site of the same class (see §3, F2).\n\n## 3. The fix (minimal, two sites, one new helper)\n\nF1 — `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/code.cljc`\n\nAdd `[dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]` to the ns requires and one private helper next\nto `with-registers`:\n\n```clojure\n(defn- tuple=\n  \"Item 13's tuple equality. Host `=` is not NaN-reflexive on JS and Dart\n   (only the JVM short-circuits on the shared box), so a NaN literal would\n   refuse its own re-projection. Slot by slot: the re-projection copies\n   literal operands by reference, so `identical?` settles them without a\n   traversal; everything else goes through the encoder's own kind-strict\n   equality, under which canonical NaNs are equal and 0.0 and -0.0 are not.\"\n  [a b]\n  (and (= (count a) (count b))\n       (every? true? (map cbor/content= a b))))\n```\n\n(`cbor/content=` already begins with `identical?`, so the slotwise form gives\nthe reference shortcut for free.) Then replace the two comparisons in\n`canonical-projection`:\n\n- line 815: `(when-not (= t (nth v pc))` → `(when-not (tuple= t (nth v pc))`\n- line 820: `(when-not (= (get canon pc) (nth v pc))` → `(when-not (tuple= (get canon pc) (nth v pc))`\n\nWhy slotwise rather than `(cbor/content= t (nth v pc))` on the whole tuple:\nthe whole-tuple form builds a `content-key` over every data literal four\ntimes per load (two sides, register pass and layout pass); the slotwise form\nhits `identical?` on the literal slot and never walks it. Either form is\ncorrect; the slotwise one is the one to ship. Do NOT compare only register\nslots in the layout pass: there the canon tuple at pc may come from another\npc of `v`, so literals must be compared, and content= does that.\n\nBehaviour notes for the rule: item 13 keeps refusing real register and layout\ndefects in NaN-carrying vectors (content= is a strict equality, F below pins\nit). A `-0.0` literal versus a `0.0` literal is now a difference (host `=`\nmerged them), which is the encoder's own notion of canonical content and is\nthe right answer for a content-addressed vector. On JS, `content-key` refuses\nan unsafe raw integral Number; such a literal could not reach `segment-key`\neither (same refusal), so no vector that loads today stops loading.\n\nF2 — `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register.cljc` line 281 (`store-image`)\n\n`(= (val existing) image)` compares two whole images (vector, bodies,\nanalysis) with host `=`. With a NaN literal this throws \"the id already holds\ndifferent code\" for a content-equal reload: on the JVM already when the box\ndiffers (probe I), on JS and Dart even for the identical vector (probe H would\nfail there). Both images under one segment id are deterministic functions of\ntheir vector, and `:address` is `jing/segment-key` (a keyword\n`:segment/blake3-<digest>` over the canonical encoding), so address equality\nis content equality. Replace with:\n\n```clojure\n(if (= (:address (val existing)) (:address image)) images ...)\n```\n\nNo helper, no traversal, host-neutral. (Alternative, if the Architect of the\ncarrier prefers vector comparison: `(cbor/content= (:vector (val existing))\n(:vector image))`. Address comparison is the one to ship.)\n\nNothing else on the load/derive/allocation path compares literal values:\nevery other `=`/`not=`/`set`/`distinct` in `code.cljc`, `derive.cljc`,\n`linearize.cljc`, `layout.cljc`, `analysis.cljc`, `scan.cljc` is over\nmnemonics, pcs, register ids, counts, symbols or kinds (surveyed by grep; the\nlist is in the orchestrator's transcript).\n\n## 4. Tests to add (portable `.cljc`, all three lanes)\n\nT1 — `test/yin/vm/semantic_register/code_test.cljc`, new deftest\n`item-13-compares-literal-operands-by-content` (keep the `refusals` table\nand `every-item-has-a-refusal-row` untouched). Accepted (`nil` from\n`code/well-formed?`):\n\n```clojure\n'[[:const 0 ##NaN] [:halt 0]]\n;; NaN in a body and in main: exercises the per-body register pass and the\n;; whole-segment layout pass\n'[[:closure 1 [x] 4] [:const 2 ##NaN] [:call 0 1 [2] false] [:halt 0]\n  [:const 0 ##NaN] [:return 0]]\n;; NaN and signed zero nested inside data operands\n'[[:const 0 [##Inf ##-Inf -0.0 0.0 ##NaN {:k ##NaN}]] [:halt 0]]\n'[[:store-put 0 {:k ##NaN} [##NaN]] [:halt 0]]\n```\n\nRefused, pinning that NaN does not mask a defect and that content= is strict:\n\n```clojure\n;; rd must be 0: the NaN literal is beside the point\n[{:rule :noncanonical-registers :pc 0} '[[:const 1 ##NaN] [:halt 1]]]\n;; (f (fn [x] NaN) (fn [y] Inf)) with its bodies swapped; the layout pass\n;; now compares [:const 0 ##NaN] against [:const 0 ##Inf] and must differ\n[{:rule :noncanonical-layout :pc 1}\n '[[:var 1 f] [:closure 2 [x] 7] [:closure 3 [y] 5] [:call 0 1 [2 3] false]\n   [:halt 0] [:const 0 ##Inf] [:return 0] [:const 0 ##NaN] [:return 0]]]\n```\n\n(Codex: verify the pc of the second refusal by running it; the existing\nswapped-bodies row reports pc 1, where the first `:closure` sits, because the\nlayout pass reports the least differing pc; the first differing tuple here\nis also at the closure site. Pin whatever `well-formed?` returns on the JVM\nafter the fix, then confirm Node and Dart agree.)\n\nThese rows fail today on Node and Dart (every accepted row above returns\n`{:rule :noncanonical-registers :pc 0}` there) and pass on the JVM, which is\nexactly the gap the lanes left open.\n\nT2 — a new deftest in `test/yin/vm/semantic_engine_test.cljc` (it already\ndrives the register kernel) `a-nan-literal-loads-runs-and-reloads`:\n\n```clojure\n(let [nan   (* 1.0 ##NaN)             ; a fresh box on the JVM, a plain NaN elsewhere\n      v1    [[:const 0 ##NaN] [:halt 0]]\n      v2    [[:const 0 nan] [:halt 0]]  ; content-equal, not identical on the JVM\n      m     (semantic/load-vector (semantic/create-vm {}) v1 code/contract)\n      value (vm/value (vm/run m))]\n  (is (not= value value) \"the kernel yields NaN\")        ; portable NaN test\n  (is (cbor/content= ##NaN value))\n  (let [m2 (semantic/load-vector m v1 code/contract)     ; identical reload (fails today on JS/Dart)\n        m3 (semantic/load-vector m v2 code/contract)]    ; content-equal reload (fails today on the JVM too)\n    (is (= (:program m) (:program m2) (:program m3)) \"one address, one segment id\")))\n```\n\nT3 — no new Python test: `yang.python.antlr.int-ops-test/nan-comparisons-test`\nand `float-division-edge-test` are the regression and go green on Node and\nDart with F1. Keep them.\n\n## 5. Other kernels and paths\n\n- `derive.cljc` (`stack-image`, `register-image`, the `:stack` and `:register`\n  runners) calls `code/parse`, not `well-formed?`; item 13 never runs there,\n  which is why those runners stayed green in 8e and 8f-3. No change.\n- `debruijn_register_code.cljc` rules (`live-exact-rule` 641, 368, 518, 550)\n  compare live sets, arities and owners: integers only. No change.\n- `debruijn_code.cljc` 233 `(not= v v)` is a deliberate NaN detector. No change.\n- `yin.vm/same-content?` (vm.cljc 1072) already uses `cbor/content=` after\n  the 8e ruling. `yin.vm.data/data-content=` likewise.\n- Known gap, OUT of this ruling's scope, for the ledger:\n  `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register/frame.cljc` 141 compares a captured\n  frame's free-environment bindings with the task's free-env by host `=`. A\n  NaN-valued free binding in a captured, parked or waiting frame would be\n  refused as `:free-env-mismatch` on JS and Dart. Same class, different layer\n  (carrier validation, not load). Fix shape when taken: slotwise content\n  equality guarded for callables and refs the way `data-content=` does.\n\n## 6. Ordered steps for codex\n\n1. In `code.cljc`: add the `dao.jing.cbor` require, add `tuple=` after\n   `with-registers`, switch lines 815 and 820 to `tuple=`. Update the\n   `canonical-projection` docstring with one sentence: tuples compare by the\n   encoder's content equality, not host `=`.\n2. In `semantic_register.cljc` `store-image`: compare `:address`, not the\n   image.\n3. Add T1 to `code_test.cljc` and T2 to `semantic_engine_test.cljc`\n   (`cbor` and `code` requires as needed).\n4. JVM: `clojure -M:test -n yin.vm.semantic-register.code-test -n\n   yin.vm.semantic-engine-test -n yang.python.antlr.int-ops-test`. Expect T2's\n   content-equal reload to have FAILED before step 2 and pass after.\n5. Node and Dart lanes for the same three namespaces (foreground, one lane at\n   a time per docs/agents/build-n-test.md); confirm \"Testing\n   yin.vm.semantic-register.code-test\" appears in the node output and that\n   `nan-comparisons-test` / `float-division-edge-test` report the Python\n   vectors, not `[:thrown ...]`.\n6. Quick tier (G1) before handing back; the design doc\n   `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md` §3.4 item 13: add one clause\n   that tuple equality is content equality (kind-strict, canonical NaN equal,\n   signed zero distinct). No other doc changes.\n7. Report path `./collab/<ms>-engineer-8f3d.report.md`, ending with the three\n   lanes' counts for the three namespaces.\n\nRULING-READY\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-10-15 10:50:57 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-15 17:50:58 +07\nCoding-Agent: claude (claude-fable-5-1)\nSession-ID: not exposed to this session (see the harness stdout log beside the prompt)\n# 8f-2 Architect review: uncommitted rename diff + ruling on the frozen old-name keywords\n\nReviewed: worktree `datomworld-srvm-p8f2`, branch `srvm-phase8f2` at `5804a1dc`, working tree uncommitted. Input: `collab/1792061140107-engineer-8f2.report.md` (codex). Read-only except this report; two scratch verifier files (a throwaway JVM test namespace and a perl script under collab) were created to get around the sandbox and deleted again; `git status` shows no residue.\n\n## Independent verification\n\n**(1) Moves are byte-identical renames; nothing else changed.** CONFIRMED. I compared every one of the 24 deleted HEAD files against its new path and every one of the 64 modified tracked files against HEAD, after applying exactly three substitutions to the HEAD side: `yin.vm.semantic-register` (not followed by `-vm`) to `yin.vm.semantic`, `yin/vm/semantic_register` to `yin/vm/semantic`, `semantic_register.cljc` to `semantic.cljc`. Result: 24 moves identical, 63 of 64 edits identical. The single residual is `src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:978`, a docstring where the alias-style API reference `semantic-register/load-ast` / `semantic-register/load-vector` became `semantic/load-ast` / `semantic/load-vector`. That is the correct new spelling of the same API reference and is covered by the brief's \"API references\" clause. No logic, whitespace or pinned literal changed anywhere.\n\n**(2) Zero live references.** CONFIRMED. `semantic[-_]register` over `src`, `test`, `bb.edn`, `deps.edn`, `shadow-cljs.edn`, `bin`, `src/dev`, `.clj-kondo`, `.github`, `package.json`, excluding the `yin.vm.semantic-register-vm*` design-doc citations, returns exactly the 74 lines the engineer tabulated: model/backend/lane keywords, prose, two deftest names, and the `semantic-registers` register-file function. Not one namespace symbol, require vector, path string or `ns-publics` lookup remains. `docs/agents/build-n-test.md:438` is prose only (no lane command names the old namespace). The only other non-doc hits are dated transcripts under `archive/`.\n\n**(3) No hashed or pinned identity moved.** CONFIRMED. Because (1) proves the diff is substitution-only, the only way a hash could move is if a hash input contained the namespace string. The two descriptor pins (`7b7c6ae9…f3489` in `debruijn_code_test.cljc:362`, `aa757659…7e74c` in `debruijn_register_code_test.cljc:11`) are untouched and the engineer's whole JVM quick tier (4005 tests, 249867 assertions, 0 failures) passed against them, which is the executable proof. The format tag stays `:yin.semantic/code`; no golden H pair or A address literal is in the diff. The `:vm/model` telemetry value is never pinned by literal: `telemetry_test.cljc:216` asserts `[model]` symbolically from the table key.\n\n**(4) The ten C4 files are the only test/yang edits, three substitutions each.** CONFIRMED. `git diff --numstat HEAD -- test/yang` lists exactly the ten permitted files, `3 3` each, and each passed the normalization compare in (1). No `src/yang` file changed.\n\nLanes: JVM quick tier and the ten C4 namespaces were run by the engineer (reported green). Node and Dart remain with the orchestrator per the brief; this is a pure rename so I do not require them before commit, but the landing rule (three hosts per slice) still applies to the 8f merge.\n\n## Ruling: the 44 \"frozen model identity and test backend/lane keyword\" lines\n\n**Decision: rename them to `:semantic` now, as a second commit inside 8f-2 (call it 8f-2b), not in 8g and not left.** Hash-free, store-free, mechanical. Reasons:\n\n1. **`:semantic` is the documented model keyword, and it is free.** The old kernel deleted in 8f-3 was the one that emitted `:vm-model :semantic` and called `(telemetry/install :semantic)` (verified at `e1f6a580:src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:936,949`). `docs/design/yin.vm.telemetry.implementation-plan.md:85,271-272` prescribes the two models as `:ast-walker` and `:semantic`. `:semantic-register` was a transitional name chosen only so the two kernels could coexist. The coexistence ended at 8f-3; the phase-8 plan's own stated goal is that the register kernel *is* the semantic kernel. Keeping `:semantic-register` in the kernel is the keyword-level equivalent of the compat shim the plan (Q3, Q6) rules out.\n2. **`:vm/model` is persisted.** `telemetry.cljc:258-268` writes the model keyword into every root snapshot datom on the telemetry stream. A transitional name leaking into durable datoms after the rename is exactly the \"legacy as a shim\" argument. Dev-only repo, no deployed stores (owner rule), so there is nothing to migrate: the cost is zero today and non-zero later.\n3. **The engineer's collision argument is inverted.** The report preserved `:semantic-register` \"to avoid colliding with the separate existing `:semantic` backend in `rule_r_test`\". That `:semantic` backend is not separate any more: since 8f-3 it builds the same kernel via `semantic/create-vm` + `semantic/load-ast` (`rule_r_test.cljc:96-100`). The same duplication exists in `continuation_invoke_test.cljc` (`:semantic-register` at 33, `:semantic` at 42), `ffi_test.cljc` (382 and 385) and `linker_require_test.cljc` (120 and 165). In `linker_require_test` the `:semantic-register` entry is additionally a stale phase-5 stub (`:obligations (constantly [])`, excluded at line 611 \"until phase 5c supplies the register-vector scanners\", which landed long ago) while the `:semantic` entry runs the real `linker/semantic-format` obligations. So the correct move in those four tables is to **delete the `:semantic-register` entry**, not rename it: the register kernel is already covered under `:semantic`, and C4 already uses `:semantic` for it (`e2e_c2_test.clj:39,1147`, `int_ops_test.cljc:46`, …). Coverage note: `continuation_invoke_test`'s `:semantic-register` runner stepped the machine with an explicit bounded `vm/step` loop; dropping it is acceptable because `test/yin/vm/semantic/vm_test.cljc` exercises `vm/step` on the kernel directly (12 call sites).\n4. **Lane labels are test-local.** `safepoint_harness_test.cljc` derives the lane from the module format tag (`lane-of`, line 130) and the `:lane` key on roots is built by the harness itself (line 1592); `src/` has no `:lane` keyword outside `src/dev/affected.clj`, which is unrelated. Neither file uses a bare `:semantic` keyword, so a global replace is collision-free. The design doc that names the lanes (`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md` §5.3 line 1115, §8.5) is 8g's; 8g must update that lane name alongside the doc rename.\n\nWhy not 8g: 8g is the documentation slice and its acceptance grep is `yin.vm.semantic-register` (the namespace), which would never catch a keyword. Why not leave: the kernel would ship under one name in `ns` and another in its own telemetry forever.\n\n### Exact edit list for codex (8f-2b; no hash, golden or `docs/design` edit)\n\nProduction:\n- `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:388` `:vm-model :semantic-register` to `:vm-model :semantic`.\n- `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:402` `(telemetry/install :semantic-register)` to `(telemetry/install :semantic)`.\n\nTelemetry test (no collision):\n- `test/yin/vm/telemetry_test.cljc:4` docstring `` `:semantic-register` `` to `` `:semantic` ``.\n- `test/yin/vm/telemetry_test.cljc:132` table key `:semantic-register` to `:semantic`.\n\nBackend tables (delete the duplicate; keep the existing `:semantic` entry untouched):\n- `test/yin/vm/rule_r_test.cljc:123-125` delete the `:semantic-register` entry; line 207 `(select-keys backends [:ast-walker :semantic :semantic-register])` to `(select-keys backends [:ast-walker :semantic])`.\n- `test/yin/vm/continuation_invoke_test.cljc:33-40` delete the `:semantic-register` runner entry (the `:semantic` runner at 42 stays).\n- `test/yin/vm/ffi_test.cljc:382-383` delete the `:semantic-register` vm-kind entry (the `:semantic` entry at 385 stays).\n- `test/yin/vm/linker_require_test.cljc:120-126` delete the `:semantic-register` backend entry including its two stub comments; line 611 `(doseq [backend (remove #{:semantic-register} (keys backends))]` to `(doseq [backend (keys backends)]` and drop the stale \"excluded until phase 5c\" comment on 610.\n\nLane labels (global replace `:semantic-register` to `:semantic`, both files verified collision-free):\n- `test/yin/vm/semantic/safepoint_harness_test.cljc` lines 2, 97, 100, 103, 126, 136, 175, 183, 1456, 1458, 1464, 1465, 1604, 1747, 1936 (15 lines; line 1604's expected vector becomes `[:semantic :stack :register]`).\n- `test/yin/vm/semantic/layout_test.cljc` lines 123, 125, 150, 300, 302, 313, 381, 419, 512, 546, 568, 576, 578, 583, 646, 660, 664, 672, 689 (19 lines).\n\nTest names (P3, same commit since the files are open anyway):\n- `test/yin/vm/linker_test.cljc:2043` `semantic-register-scanners-yield-position-bearing-records` to `semantic-scanners-yield-position-bearing-records`; `:2056` `semantic-register-format-refuses-a-malformed-vector` to `semantic-format-refuses-a-malformed-vector`.\n\nVerification for 8f-2b: `clojure -M:test -e :slow -n yin.vm.telemetry-test -n yin.vm.rule-r-test -n yin.vm.continuation-invoke-test -n yin.vm.ffi-test -n yin.vm.linker-require-test -n yin.vm.linker-test -n yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test -n yin.vm.semantic.layout-test`, then the whole JVM quick tier, then `git grep -n ':semantic-register' -- src test` must return nothing. Pinned descriptor hashes must still read `7b7c6ae9…f3489` and `aa757659…7e74c`.\n\nNot part of this ruling: `continuation_handoff.cljc:178,207` `semantic-registers` (the register file, correct as is); `vm-key->model` there returns `:ast-walker` and is unaffected.\n\n## Other leftover names that will confuse after the rename\n\n- **P2, for 8g's scope statement.** Nine code docstrings cite `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm*.md` by file name (`semantic/analysis.cljc:3`, `semantic/code.cljc:3`, `semantic/linearize.cljc:3`, `semantic/layout.cljc:2`, `ucf/rows.cljc:233`, `test/yin/vm/semantic/corpus.cljc:2`, `layout_test.cljc:2`, `safepoint_harness_test.cljc:3`, `ucf/rows_test.cljc:359`). When 8g renames the docs (Q6 option c) these become dangling, so 8g must be allowed to touch these src/test lines even though it is \"docs only\". Record that in the 8g brief.\n- **P3, prose pass (8g or 8f-2b, codex's choice).** 17 src lines and 6 test lines still say \"semantic-register machine/kernel/evaluator/VM\" in prose (`semantic/layout.cljc:18,28,716,760,781,789,954`; `ucf/rows.cljc:4,1321,1736,2245`; `stack_parity_test.cljc:6,120`; `safepoint_harness_test.cljc:1716`; `rows_support.cljc:3`; `rows_checkpoint_fixtures.cljc:7`; `ucf/holder/export_test.cljc:5`). Replace with \"semantic machine/kernel\". Also `semantic/layout.cljc:4,20` say \"register machine\" / \"the register kernel\" meaning this kernel (not the de Bruijn register backend), which is now genuinely ambiguous; say \"the semantic kernel\".\n- **P3, record name.** `semantic.cljc:16` `defrecord RegisterVM` with the diagnostic \"The register VM executes loaded vectors; use load-ast\" (line 335, no test pins the message). `SemanticVM` was the deleted record's name and is now free. Rename in the prose pass; it is a symbol, not an identity (no `pr-str` of the record is persisted: UCF rows carry fields, not