{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git log --oneline --all --grep='phase 5\\\\|phase 4\\\\|phase 7\\\\|phase 6' -35; rg -n 'malformed-vectors' test/yin/vm; rg -n 'SHA-256|sha256' docs/design/yin.vm.linker.md docs/design/yin.vm.debruijn*.md; sed -n '915,949p' src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/layout.cljc; sed -n '655,675p' docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md\"","aggregated_output":"2c70bec1 docs(orchestrator-log): semantic-register-vm seat handoff, phase 7 landed, phase 8 slices 8ab and 8d in flight\n67b98907 Merge branch 'srvm-phase7': custody on rows, the rows inspector, the holder's export and recovery format 2, composition and fencing over row packs, Stage E over the semantic-register kernel, phase 7 documentation\n00243b57 fix(yin.vm.ucf): a non-BLAKE3 carrier row id is refused undecodable, the install image negative isolated (phase 7 merge review)\n6fc65722 fix(yin.vm.ucf): carried addresses verify under their own algorithm, the scanner golden for the C4 python group regenerated (merged phase 7)\ne6337294 Merge master into srvm-phase7m (conflicting doc hunks: the phase 7e wording)\n627272d7 Merge branch 'srvm-phase7e' into srvm-phase7: phase 7 documentation (phase 7e)\n699b0c60 Merge branch 'srvm-phase7d' into srvm-phase7: Stage E over semantic-register row packs (phase 7d)\nfdd6ce74 docs(yin.vm.ucf): the de Bruijn backends are retained, lower-defect and harness exclusions stated exactly, fixture claims corrected (phase 7e review)\n32a98db1 docs(yin.vm.ucf): phase 7 documentation, custody by kind, the lower stages, recovery format 2, pack address and root, backends wording (phase 7e)\n8aa148be test(yin.vm.ucf): Stage E over semantic-register row packs, reversed-row variant, source index seam, pack re-emission across hosts (phase 7d)\n02f63946 Merge branch 'srvm-phase7c' into srvm-phase7: composition and fencing over row packs (phase 7c)\n05d3a25f test(yin.vm.ucf): composition and fencing suites over row packs, recovery before the pack asserted, install record address isolated (phase 7c)\ndbf62732 Merge branch 'srvm-phase7b' into srvm-phase7: the holder exports row packs, recovery format 2, the driver lowers rows, install checks (phase 7b)\n95c228c0 feat(yin.vm.ucf): the holder exports row packs, recovery format 2, the driver lowers rows, install checks (phase 7b)\n4376b033 Merge branch 'srvm-phase7a' into srvm-phase7: custody on rows, the rows inspector, the authority's fixtures (phase 7a)\nb4d80e8d feat(yin.vm.ucf): custody on rows, the rows inspector and the authority's fixtures over row packs (phase 7a)\n30730c51 test(yin.vm.semantic-register): scoped native layout worlds, guarded law-4 controls, nested free-environment refusals, receiver image functions pinned (phase 6c review)\ndc545aaa fix(yin.vm.semantic-register): layout refusals for ambiguous images and free-environment procedures, law-4 controls, an ambiguous virt refusal, audit allowlist (phase 6c review)\n47ddb1d9 feat(yin.vm.semantic-register): the register and stack layouts and the cross-engine lanes of the safepoint harness (phase 6c)\nbafdec74 test(yin.vm.semantic-register): a closure inside a module-store value must name a carried store (phase 6b review)\nf650e046 fix(yin.vm.ucf): every store-of names a module store of its own task, dependency discharge follows control flow from the resume pc (phase 6b review)\na396f996 fix(yin.vm.ucf): task lower refuses carrier defects before any attachment, per-context dependency discharge, install records checked (phase 6b review)\nc3d37586 feat(yin.vm.ucf): full task transport, lift-task and lower-task, and the safepoint harness on the reference lane (phase 6b)\n19f8a1d2 feat(yin.vm.ucf): cursor cells are numbered by discovery order, sorted sets and maps, a tie test and a refusal (phase 6a)\nd77da9f0 refactor(yin.vm.ucf): the carrier's box is a cursor cell; regenerate the pinned root ids (phase 6a)\n83fd51d8 refactor(yin.vm.ucf): rename the carrier's cell to cursor, regenerate the pinned root ids (phase 6a)\naf2b29c4 fix(yin.vm.ucf): input row bodies do not spend the label-byte budget (phase 6a review)\n6b7e65ed fix(yin.vm.ucf): refuse guest marker shapes in every literal context, tag decoded equality, bound label bytes (phase 6a review)\n5e6c6f79 test(yin.vm.semantic-register): pin the widened-start rule with an observable program (phase 5b review)\n296f75fd Merge branch 'srvm-phase6cpre': the stack kernel delivers tail-call effect results through K (phase 6c-pre)\nb2eadc83 feat(yin.vm.semantic-register): A to R, linear-scan allocation over A's liveness (phase 5b)\n290c4476 test(yin.vm.linker): cover the v4 format record and its registration (phase 5c review)\nbb4a6558 fix(yin.vm.ucf): refuse malformed census keys, installs and marker collisions, and kill the surviving mutants (phase 6a review)\n7e1f1e89 test(yin.vm.debruijn): pin the empty-K halt value and store context and the inner return pc (phase 6c-pre review)\n58dc0964 feat(yin.vm.semantic-register): the v4 scanners and the production linker format record (phase 5c)\ntest/yin/vm/malformed_rows.cljc:54:(def malformed-vectors\ntest/yin/vm/semantic/scan_test.cljc:214:(deftest malformed-vectors-throw\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:239:It uses `jing/blake3` (SHA-256 until the phase-8 cutover, 2026-10-15;\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:298:BLAKE3 (SHA-256 until the phase-8 cutover, 2026-10-15) and is pinned by the\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:359:pinned to explicit BLAKE3 (SHA-256 until the phase-8 cutover, 2026-10-15;\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md:174:(SHA-256 until the phase-8 cutover, 2026-10-15; the descriptor's `:hash`\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md:277:Implement the descriptor-based SHA-256 encoder (BLAKE3 since the\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn-projection.md:353:the domain separator and BLAKE3 is the hash (SHA-256 until the phase-8\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:288:> 8ab (`:hash :blake3`; \"pinned to SHA-256 by contract freeze\" below is\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:289:> historical), and SHA-256 remains only dao.jing's explicitly mintable\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:316:  pinned to SHA-256 by contract freeze, independent of the storage\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:382:  `:sha256` while the default is `:blake3` verifies under the algorithm\ndocs/design/yin.vm.linker.md:2212:under `:sha256` verifies against its own address while the default is\n\n(defn lower-defect\n  \"What a kernel of `kind` cannot hold, judged on decoded task `task`\n   before anything is attached: two carried A of one image (§4.1), install\n   children (not carried by this phase's layouts), a closure or\n   continuation in the free environment (§6.3), and for the register\n   kernel a primitive function in the payload data of a wait or parked\n   state (a window, a lexical binding, or reached through them), which\n   its restore refuses as `:continuation-registers` (`vm/machine-data?`).\n   nil when it can.\"\n  [task kind]\n  (let [slots (:slots task)\n        code (nth slots 11)\n        collision (image-collision code kind)\n        free (free-env-procedure task)]\n    (cond\n      collision\n      (assoc {} :yin.k/status :yin.k/unsupported :yin.k/kind :ambiguous-image\n             :yin.k/image (first collision) :yin.k/segments (second collision))\n\n      (seq (nth slots 12))\n      (assoc {} :yin.k/status :yin.k/unsupported :yin.k/kind :installs)\n\n      free\n      (assoc {} :yin.k/status :yin.k/unsupported :yin.k/kind :free-env-value :yin.k/path free)\n\n      (= :register kind)\n      (when-let [path (or (some (fn [[i w]] (state-prim code (first (:slots w)) [:frames i]))\n                                (map-indexed vector (nth slots 13)))\n                          (some (fn [[p st]] (state-prim code st [:parked p]))\n                                (partition 2 (:slots (nth slots 8)))))]\n        (assoc {} :yin.k/status :yin.k/unsupported :yin.k/kind :continuation-registers :yin.k/path path))\n\n      :else nil)))\n\n## §7.4 Safepoints — where a canonical configuration exists (blocker 1)\n\n### 7.4.1 Only safepoints lift, and the table is the machine's\n\nSuperseded for the register-shaped machine by\n`yin.vm.semantic.md` §4.1 (two state columns, `act` and\n`tail`, and the `deliver` record); the table below describes the\nstack-shaped machine, which left at that design's phase 8 (2026-10-15),\nand the stack-shaped halves of the old `yin.vm.ucf` that served it —\nthe safepoint table, `stack-effect`, `parking-kinds` — were deleted\nwith it, un-ported (8f-1 ruling R2); the register machine's safepoint\nfacts live in `yin.vm.semantic.md` §4 and the frame validator of\n`yin.vm.semantic.frame`.\n\nThe linear machine's registers are canonical only *between* instructions.\nInside a `:call` that has popped its operands but not yet pushed a frame, or\ninside a superinstruction the loader fused (§6.4), no ⟨C, E, S, K⟩ exists\nthat both describes the state and is expressible in the §2.4 vocabulary.\nUCF resolves this by rule rather than by metadata: **a continuation may be\nlifted only at a safepoint**, and a safepoint is a transition of the\nreference machine at which the machine parks. The first draft's table\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
