{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport subprocess\np=Path('src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/bytecode-vm-optimization.md')\np.write_bytes(subprocess.check_output(['git','show','HEAD:'+str(p)]))\ndef edit(name, a,b):\n p=Path(name);s=p.read_text();assert a in s,(name,a);p.write_text(s.replace(a,b))\nbase='docs/design/'\nedit(base+'yin.vm.semantic.md','**History.**','<a id=\\\"history\\\"></a>\\\\n\\\\n**History.**')\nedit(base+'yin.vm.semantic.md','contracts \"'`\"v2\"` then `\"v3\"`),'\"','contracts \"'`\"v2\"` then `\"v3\"`; revision 1, 2026-09-18, published'\"\\\\n\"'`\"v2\"`, and revision 2, 2026-09-25, published `\"v3\"` with `:define`'\"\\\\nand the reserved name \"'`yin/def`),'\"')\nedit(base+'yin.vm.semantic.md','That document\\\\'s §1 held this design\\\\'s stance avant la lettre —','That document\\\\'s §1 stated the same stance —')\nedit(base+'yin.vm.semantic.md','Eight phases, each gated; the old evaluator survives only as an oracle\\\\nuntil phase 8.','Eight phases, each gated. The dated migration record below retains the\\\\ncoexistence names: the old evaluator survived as an oracle until phase 8\\\\n(2026-10-15).')\nedit(base+'yin.vm.semantic.md','digest everywhere in yin.vm except SHA-256 explicitly minted in\\\\n   dao.jing.','digest throughout \"'`yin.vm`; `dao.jing` still permits explicit SHA-256'\"\\\\n   minting.)'.replace('.)', '.'))\nedit(base+'yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md','\"'`\"v2\"` then `\"v3\"`) was deleted, its §1 stance and this revision'\"\\\\nhistory preserved in the new document\\\\'s history block.','\"'`\"v2\"` then `\"v3\"`) was deleted. Its revision 1 (2026-09-18; status'\"\\\\ncorrected 2026-09-25) published \"'`\"v2\"`; revision 2 (2026-09-25)'\"\\\\npublished \"'`\"v3\"`, adding `:define` and the reserved name `yin/def`'\"\\\\n(the landed contract change is I-4 above). Its §1 stance was: everything\\\\nis a stream, with instruction fetch inside a loaded segment deliberately\\\\nexcepted; interpretation creates semantics; code and state are datoms;\\\\neverything is a continuation. It enforced the six invariants: no hidden\\\\nglobal state, implicit control flow, callbacks, shared mutable state,\\\\nlayer collapsing or assumed graphs. This stance and the revision dates\\\\nare preserved in the new document\\\\'s [history block](./yin.vm.semantic.md#history).')\nedit(base+'yin.vm.dependency-completion.md','Never implemented as\\\\n> designed: the dependency-closure walk this document specifies is\\\\n> \"'`yin.vm.semantic.scan` (the scanners over the v4 table) and the lift'\"\\\\'s\\\\n> completion side is the engine\\\\'s \"'`lift-slice`;'\"','The surviving\\\\n> dependency facts are computed by \"'`yin.vm.semantic.scan` (the scanners'\"\\\\n> over the v4 table), and the lift\\\\'s completion side is the engine\\\\'s\\\\n> \"'`lift-slice`;'\"')\nfor n in ['stack','register']:\n edit(base+f'yin.vm.debruijn.{n}.md','on that fragment and refusing the unsupported remainder before attach.','on that fragment. Refusal of the unsupported remainder before attach\\\\n> remains the requirement; §4.6 lists the four implemented checks and the\\\\n> harness-only exclusions, not a general fragment gate.')\nedit(base+'yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md','The stack and register kernels are the canonical kernel\\\\'s two\\\\n  backends, checked on their documented fragment and required to refuse the','Use the canonical kernel and its two backends, checked on the\\\\n  documented fragment and required to refuse the')\nedit(base+'yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md','backend fragment). They are retained','backend fragment, including the implemented checks and harness-only\\\\n  exclusions; there is no general pre-attach fragment gate). They are retained')\nedit(base+'yin.vm.linker.md','pinned to SHA-256 by contract freeze, independent of the storage','pinned to BLAKE3 since phase 8 (SHA-256 before the 2026-10-15\\\\n  cutover), independent of the storage')\nedit(base+'yin.vm.linker.md','8ab (\"'`:hash :blake3`; \"pinned to SHA-256 by contract freeze\" below is'\"\\\\n> historical),','8ab (\"'`:hash :blake3`),'\"')\nedit(base+'yin.vm.semantic.derivations.md','live \"'`\"v3\"` comparisons went with the old scanners at 8e'\"','live \"'`\"v3\"` comparisons were removed at 8f-1; the old scanners'\"\\\\nwent with the stack table at 8f-3')\nedit(base+'yin.vm.semantic.derivations.md','and \"'`semantic-format` (§7.5) for `v4`'\"','and the then \"'`semantic-register-format` (§7.5) for `v4`'\"')\nedit(base+'yin.vm.semantic.derivations.md','**PROPOSED.** Phase 8 deletes the \"'`\"v3\"` scanners'\"','**Original proposal (2026-10-11).** Phase 8 deletes the \"'`\"v3\"` scanners'\"')\nedit(base+'yin.vm.semantic.derivations.md','evaluator design §3.3), **PROPOSED** scanner bindings:','evaluator design §3.3); implemented scanner bindings, with names\\\\nupdated at the 2026-10-15 cutover:')\nedit(base+'yin.vm.semantic.derivations.md','Added to \"'`linker.cljc` beside `semantic-format`'\"','Originally added as \"'`semantic-register-format` to `linker.cljc` beside'\"\\\\nthe old \"'`semantic-format`'\"')\nedit(base+'yin.vm.semantic.derivations.md','**DECIDED** today: \"'`publish-closure!`'\"','**Coexistence record (2026-10-11).** \"'`publish-closure!`'\"')\nedit(base+'yin.vm.semantic.derivations.md','The C4 manifest goldens were regenerated once more at 8ab\\\\n(the BLAKE3 descriptors) and at 8f, over the newly published images.','The BLAKE3 descriptor regeneration was 8ab; the C4 manifest\\\\ngoldens were refreshed at 8f over the newly published images.')\nedit(base+'yin.vm.semantic.derivations.md','**DECIDED** by ruling 2 and the reviewer\\\\'s finding. Both descriptors','**Historical rationale (2026-10-11),** ruling 2 and the reviewer\\\\'s\\\\nfinding. Both descriptors')\nedit(base+'yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md','renamed kernel; versions 0/1/2 and their codecs died with the old\\\\ntransport in 8f-1','new kernel (renamed at 8f-2); the old codec tests and fixtures died\\\\nin 8d, and their transport sources in 8f-1')\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
