{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"head -16 docs/design/yin.vm.v2.divergence-register.md; rg --files docs | rg 'implementation-plan|yin.vm.v2'; rg -n 'yin.vm.semantic-register|semantic-register-vm' docs/design; sed -n '1187,1200p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md; sed -n '205,225p' test/yin/vm/semantic/scan_test.cljc; rg -n 'malformed-rows|malformed-vectors' test src --glob '\"'!yang/**'\"'; git diff --check; git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"# yin.vm — the divergence register\n\nStatus: deliverable of phase V6 of\n[`yin.vm.implementation-plan.md`](./yin.vm.implementation-plan.md),\namended by its phase V7. Subordinate to [`dao.stream.md`](./dao.stream.md)\nand [`datom.world.md`](./datom.world.md).\n\nEvery place `yin.vm` deliberately differs from `yin.vm`, with the reason.\nSaying which v1 behaviours are deliberately not mirrored *is* the register: a\nv2 suite that \"covers the same programs\" proves nothing unless the places it\ncannot cover are named.\n\nThe sections below record the original V6 baseline except where a *V7* note\namends them: V7 moved program observation out of the VM (see\n[Program observation](#program-observation)), obsoleted the `:in-stream`\nconstruction option, and decoupled direct `eval` from queued program input.\ndocs/design/dao.lease.implementation-plan.md\ndocs/design/yin.vm.v2.divergence-register.md\ndocs/design/dao.stream.remote.implementation-plan.md\ndocs/design/dao.stream.waitset.implementation-plan.md\ndocs/design/dao.jing.remote.implementation-plan.md\ndocs/design/yin.vm.code-as-tuples.implementation-plan.md\ndocs/design/yin.vm.telemetry.implementation-plan.md\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.evaluator.md:41:(2026-10-10) it was `yin.vm.semantic-register`, beside the old\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.evaluator.md:1510:> **Evaluator.** `yin.vm.semantic-register` beside `yin.vm.semantic`.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:62:> (`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md`, forthcoming; landed and renamed\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.stack.md:65:> `collab/1791510000000-architect-semantic-register-vm.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md`.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:5:`collab/1791510000000-architect-semantic-register-vm.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md`\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:10:`semantic-register-vm` (this file was\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:11:`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md`); the phase-8 cutover (2026-10-15)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:79:> with virtual registers. once we build semantic-register-vm we can\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:80:> delete semantic-vm and rename semantic-register-vm to sematic-vm\")\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:1085:4. **Evaluator.** `yin.vm.semantic-register` beside `yin.vm.semantic`.\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md:1168:   `yin.vm.semantic-register` to `yin.vm.semantic`, remove the old H/R\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.targets.md:29:> (`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md`, forthcoming; landed and renamed\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:133:   `yin.vm.semantic-register`, its name until the phase-8 cutover) and\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:43:> vector (Architect, `collab/1791510000000-architect-semantic-register-vm.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md`\ndocs/design/yin.vm.debruijn.register.md:49:> (`yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.md`, forthcoming; landed and renamed\n   record are `:semantic`/`SemanticVM` (8f-2b); the old transport\n   sources and the v3 halves of `yin.vm.ucf` died in 8f-1 rather than\n   8d, and `yin.vm.completion` with them; item 13's tuple equality is\n   the encoder's content equality so NaN literals load on JS and Dart\n   (8f-3d); the two native kernels remain as backends over the\n   documented fragment (continuation design §4.6). BLAKE3 is the\n   digest throughout `yin.vm`; `dao.jing` still permits explicit SHA-256\n   minting.)*\n\n## 11. Questions resolved by the freeze review\n\nAll four were answered by the Architect (phase-2 review, item 10) and\nthe answers are adopte