tor-log.md:11235:Done: Landed L-d (`d0920f2b`), the dht-end-to-end trust fix (`08a3a722`), the AL-4 nits (`28ce8249`, fable APPROVE-WITH-NITS, quick tier only known failures), adopted the Q6 review rule and started `docs/agents/known-gaps.md` (owner 2026-10-14), relayed the linker-relocation note and the scan-test golden mismatch to `yin.vm.semantic-register`. Fable's I4 scoping design is in `collab/1792341000000-architect-i4-scoping.claude-fable-5-1.stdout.log` (try-require as data, registry pin invariant, derived eagerness, five slices L-d-1..L-d-3, I4-a, I4-b).\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:11242:Coding-Agent: Claude Sonnet 5.5 (interactive orchestrator seat for the UCF / `yin.vm.semantic-register-vm` track; the other seat is yang.python/C4 admission)\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:11248:Done: The register-shaped canonical semantic VM `yin.vm.semantic-register` (A the only code identity; R and H are checksums derived from A; the AST is never lost) is built and landed through phase 7: 4a/4b kernel, 5a-5c lowerers and scanners, 6a row codec + frame validator + discovery-order cursor cell numbering, 6b `lift-task`/`lower-task`, 6c layouts + cross-engine laws (61 law-4 cases, 350 law-5 transfers on the native lanes; the reference lane runs the full 89), the retention seam (`free-env` field), BLAKE3 for seals/owner tag/profile digest/DHT cookie/CBOR fixtures/ANTLR manifest, phase 7 (custody on rows, rows inspector, holder export + recovery format 2, driver lower, install checks, compose/fencing/Stage E over row packs; the Stage E process matrix ran on jupiter over four host pairs with 196 SIGKILLed lives), the phase 7 docs, and repairs of two reds in our seat after the other seat's linker relocation (the address-validation lint in `rows.cljc`; the `[:c4 :py]` scanner golden regenerated mechanically). Gates on the landed head: jupiter quick tier 13/13, Node 153 tests, Dart +126, slow tier green, post-merge quick tier green.\ndocs/orchestrator-log.md:11250:Decisions (owner): for