{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport subprocess,datetime,time\nroot=Path.cwd()\ndef run(args):\n r=subprocess.run(args,text=True,capture_output=True);return r.returncode,r.stdout+r.stderr\ndef block(args):\n rc,out=run(args);return '\"'$ '\"'+' '.join(args)+'\\\\n'+(out or '(no output)\\\\n')+f'Exit: {rc}\\\\n'\nnow=datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc)\np=Path('collab')/f'{int(time.time()*1000)}-writer-8g-codex.report.md'\nreport=f'''Completed-GMT: {now.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S GMT')}\nCompleted-Local: {now.astimezone(datetime.timezone(datetime.timedelta(hours=7))).strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S +07')}\nCoding-Agent: codex (gpt-6.1-sol)\nSession-ID: not exposed to this session (provider-generated; see adjacent harness log)\n# 8g documentation completion and verification\n\nWorktree: {root}; branch srvm-phase8g; HEAD 9fab76c6. Uncommitted and unstaged. No delegation or external messages. This report is the sole new collab artifact; existing collab inputs were not edited.\n\n## Inherited work versus this pass\n\nGLM had performed the five-document rename/replacement, most namespace substitutions, all nine permitted citation-line edits, the section-10 Met notes, UCF backend/removal notes, derivations and continuation status additions, hash prose changes, linker amendments, and known-gaps rows. All were audited against HEAD, the five supplied Architect reports, the original task and live code. The four new companion files were compared against their HEAD predecessors after normalizing names, so substantive additions were reviewed separately from rename noise.\n\nCodex corrected historical/current namespace collisions, complete source/test paths in the companions, the scanner-deletion timeline, phase-4/5 dates against git history, explicit v2/v3 revision dates and Rule R additions in both history surfaces, ambiguous v3 citations, and the overstated native pre-attach refusal claim. Removed unsupported precision about a regeneration script/count, using the actual 8ab commit instead. Removed the inherited extra edit in src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/bytecode-vm-optimization.md to obey the nine-line-only source scope. Added historical-prose ledger coverage instead. Removed a pre-existing dangling relative link to the deleted yin.vm.implementation-plan.md in the touched divergence register and identified it as historical prose.\n\n## Per-item acceptance\n\n| Item | Status and result |\n|---|---|\n| 1: Q6(c), five doc names, old stance/history, nine citations, old semantic citers | DONE. Frozen design occupies yin.vm.semantic.md; four companion moves retained, old five paths absent. Explicit history anchor preserves stance and revision 1 (2026-09-18, v2) / revision 2 (2026-09-25, v3, :define and yin/def). UCF revision I-6 repeats stance and dates, distinguishes the landed I-4 contract change, and records transport-source deletion in 8f-1. Nine source/test edits are exactly the citation substitution, byte-identical otherwise. |\n| 2: namespace/var citations | DONE. Every live citation uses yin.vm.semantic. Remaining old-name matches are dated history/quotes, listed verbatim below. Historical orchestrator-log entries were preserved. |\n| 3: UCF 7.11, 7.3, 7.4 | DONE. Uses “the canonical kernel and its two backends”, points to continuation 4.6, preserves the fixed fragment, distinguishes the four implemented checks from harness exclusions. Old 7.3 canonicalizer and 7.4 stack safepoint halves explicitly removed un-ported (ruling R2; executed in 8f-3). |\n| 4: frozen section 10 | DONE. Phases 4-7 have Met notes; phase-4/5 dates checked against 44fbafb4, 993d5411, 71b4f4d7, 5e6c6f79, 290c4476. Item 6 states owner-accepted 61/350 versus reference 89/534. Item 7 records other-seat pre-existing Dart dht-end-to-end failure. Item 8 marked met with surviving backend and BLAKE3 facts. |\n| 5: derivations, continuation, linker, completion, hashes | DONE. Statuses at derivations 7.4-8.3 and continuation 8.4 distinguish original plans from completed steps. Native by-identity fetch, publish\"'! and index-from-datoms still use H/R as checksum keys; A remains code identity. Linker 5.2 is explicitly historical v3, with current v4 record and loader named; dependency list uses semantic.code/well-formed?. Completion marked superseded by scan + lift-slice, without claiming it never existed. Stack lowerer and B-plan sections marked historical; stack grammar is debruijn-code’s own data. All current de Bruijn hash claims match BLAKE3 code. build-n-test has no moved command/namespace and was left unchanged. |\n| 6: known-gaps | DONE. Register derivation-prose gap closed; native binder defence reduction open; host-= free-env NaN gap open; dead malformed-vectors fixture open; completion/UCF deletion ledger recorded. Historical source prose outside the nine-line allowance recorded without editing it. Inherited closure rows for scanner golden and address lint agree with phase-7 git history (6fc65722, 00243b57). |\n\n## Citation judgments and inventory\n\nThe prompt’s counts are estimates from an earlier revision. On this HEAD, git grep finds old semantic-register citations in 12 design files plus the dated orchestrator log (13 total); the old semantic.md name occurs in 9 files, including the log and the to-be-replaced frozen design. No matching file was skipped because the brief estimated 17 or 25 citers.\n\n- agents/format: replace obsolete v3 border-table example with UCF (still has border tables).\n- code-as-tuples: old segment/opcode/flattening/well-formedness/cost/trace references now explicitly target the deleted-v3 history anchor; live v4 validator references remain on new 3.4. Its opening amendment identifies the historical sections. Instruction-grammar completion remains dated history.\n- code-as-tuples.implementation-plan: opening link targets v3 history; dated work-item citations are covered by its cutover note, rather than silently interpreting old section numbers as new sections.\n- engine: park/resume citation maps old 3.5 to current section 5.\n- frozen semantic design: old core vocabulary and replaced rules are labeled deleted v3; history replaces the old self-link. Current 2.3/3.3/3.4 and 4.x citations refer to the new design. Migration names remain dated coexistence history.\n- ucf-revisions: old section-number quotations remain historical, with the header and I-6 explicitly identifying the deleted referent. This is the historical contract authority, not a claim that the new 2.4 contains the old table.\n- UCF: original Phase-0 foundation points to history; old park/configuration/index/segment references are labeled v3, with current scheduler 5, configuration 2.1, safepoints 4.1 and revision-history pointers where relevant. Existing v4 amendments point to the new sections.\n- v2.divergence-register: dated v1/v2 measurements and the comparison section refer to deleted v3 history, not the unrelated new section 8.\n- orchestrator-log: every old name is inside dated append-only history; left byte-identical.\n- debruijn stack/register/targets: retain the explicitly dated 2026-10-10 “forthcoming” amendment as history, with the final name/date supplied. No live Markdown destination targets a moved file.\n- companion evaluator/derivations/continuation/cursor numbering: rename the companion references throughout; preserve commit-qualified old paths and amendment quotations as history. Full source/test paths and runnable lint paths use the new names. Evaluator 1.1 explicitly distinguishes the old stack kernel from the renamed current kernel.\n\nJudgment calls: backend refusal is a requirement, not evidence of a general fragment gate; layout/lower-defect has four checks and the harness excludes further rows. Native images still have checksum-based lookup keys, despite A-only code identity; this task documents that residue rather than claiming it vanished. Completion was implemented then deleted, so “never implemented” was removed. UCF removal was ordered by 8f-1 R2 but deferred to 8f-3 step 4b; docs now distinguish ruling from deletion. The nine-line allowance takes precedence over broader prose cleanup suggested by the review; opcase optimisation-note prose and checkpoint replacement prose are ledgered, not changed. SHA-256 registry/address examples remain valid for explicitly minted dao.jing content; only actual VM hash formulas changed.\n\n## Code evidence and verification limits\n\nRead live debruijn_code.cljc (literal table, descriptor :hash :blake3, descriptor-hash/image-hash), debruijn_register_code.cljc (descriptor/register-hash), debruijn.cljc (dimension-hash/node-hash), linker.cljc (native format identity-fn, address-attribute, index-from-datoms, publish!, semantic-format), linker/publish.cljc (tree→A, A→H/R, format-keyed manifest index), ucf.cljc (only code-address), semantic/frame.cljc (host = free-env comparison), semantic/layout.cljc (four lower-defect checks), semantic/scan_test.cljc and safepoint_harness_test.cljc (agreement and matrix counts), and vm.cljc’s projection :slot-kind rules. Confirmed no malformed/malformed-vectors reader; similarly named scanner test uses its own inline vector.\n\nHistorical lane outcomes (Stage E 196 killed lives, slow tier, the Dart failure classification) are documented from the supplied Architect/phase handoff evidence, not newly rerun here. This docs-only pass ran the explicitly requested lint/grep/link checks, not phase-8 full runtime or C4 lanes. Fable’s independent doc review remains the next workflow step; no commit/stage was performed.\n\n## Acceptance grep outputs\n\n'\"'''\nfor args in [['grep','-rn','yin.vm.semantic-register','docs','src','test'],['grep','-rn','semantic-register-vm','docs','src','test'],['grep','-rn','-i','sha256','src/cljc/yin/vm']]:\n report+='\"'```text'\"\\\\n'+block(args)+'\"'```'\"\\\\n\\\\n'\nreport+='All retained matches above are historical: dated log entries, 2026-10-10 owner/review artifact names and quotes, dated migration/coexistence records, or the 2026-10-15 rename history. No src/test match remains.\\\\n\\\\n## Other checks\\\\n\\\\n\"'```text'\"\\\\n'\nreport+=Path('/tmp/8g-link-check.txt').read_text()+'\\\\n'\nreport+='9/9 source/test files equal HEAD after only yin.vm.semantic-register-vm → yin.vm.semantic in the citation.\\\\nIndex empty; src/yang and test/yang unchanged.\\\\n'\nreport+='clojure -M:kondo --lint src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/analysis.cljc src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/code.cljc src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/linearize.cljc src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic/layout.cljc src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc test/yin/vm/semantic/corpus.cljc test/yin/vm/semantic/layout_test.cljc test/yin/vm/semantic/safepoint_harness_test.cljc test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc\\\\nLoading initial Timbre config from: :default\\\\nlinting took 2347ms, errors: 0, warnings: 0\\\\nExit: 0\\\\n'\nreport+=block(['git','diff','--check'])+'\"'```'\"\\\\n\\\\n## Diff summary\\\\n\\\\nPlain git diff --stat omits the four untracked new companion files; these are present on disk and were included in every doc/link audit. The apparent large deletes are the unstaged document moves. No git mv was used because that would stage, contrary to the brief.\\\\n\\\\n\"'```text'\"\\\\n'+block(['git','diff','--stat'])+'\"'```'\"\\\\n\\\\nNothing undecidable remains for the requested documentation pass. Existing functional gaps remain explicitly open; no coverage or runtime fix is claimed.\\\\n\\\\nREADY\\\\n'\np.write_text(report)\nprint(p)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
